{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T17:01:33.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-nhauur"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Refusal recovery bundles echo URL credentials verbatim: attempted_command and normalized_args repeat a credentialed package source on stdout and in logs"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-08 during the CodeRabbit review of PR 1688. redactSensitiveCommandArgs (src/sdk/command-line.ts) redacts only history redact invocations. Every other refusal copies the raw argv into recovery.attempted_command and recovery.normalized_args, so a package source carrying URL credentials is repeated verbatim in the structured error on stdout, in CI logs and in any agent transcript. Reproduced with the built CLI and a fake credential. 'pm package install https://u:fake-secret@example.invalid/x.tgz --project --dry-run --bogus-flag --json' fails with unknown_option, and its attempted_command contains u:fake-secret. 'pm package --catalog --install <same> --output-limit 2' fails with read_output_mutation_conflict and shows the same echo. PR 1688 already withholds that refusal's executable retry for such an argv (pm-rrwh2o), so its recovery adds no further copy; the general echo predates that change. Telemetry already strips URL userinfo through stripUrlCredentials and redactUrlsInText in src/core/telemetry/policy.ts, but the CLI recovery path does not use them. Duplicate check: searched recovery attempted_command credentials url secret redact package source; pm-m0fh (closed) covered tracked files, not runtime refusal output."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","packages","privacy","recovery","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-08T17:01:33.697Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T17:01:33.697Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every CLI recovery representation (attempted_command, normalized_args, provided_fields, suggested_retry and suggested_retry_args) removes URL userinfo from every token, or withholds an executable retry when removing it would change the command's meaning; a spec drives an unknown_option refusal and a read_output_mutation_conflict refusal with a credentialed package source and asserts that no secret appears in stdout or stderr; history redact keeps its existing flag-value redaction"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-m0fh","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-08T17:01:33.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-rrwh2o","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-08T17:01:33.697Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b900b02ccc07cfd72bee648893e108a713d5991163e3a01e9fd2779fc79bbe08","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"64bbd4b3c8093449622063063919b2b51773bb6bc45b5fe1f73ab3aa65fe1fc7"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T17:01:47.779Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T17:01:47.779Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Refusal recovery output names a credentialed package source without its userinfo, and no secret appears in stdout or stderr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"attempted_command and normalized_args repeat https://u:fake-secret@example.invalid/x.tgz verbatim for unknown_option and read_output_mutation_conflict refusals"}],"before_hash":"b900b02ccc07cfd72bee648893e108a713d5991163e3a01e9fd2779fc79bbe08","after_hash":"73bb8e8926183116cc9bd6e33405588f73b285a1d0fc41289cac9ec945a09c3d","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1e07607d54c290d67be86079cf7ae232d986890075ef736ef31f723adac57d9f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T17:32:56.017Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T17:32:56.017Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-08T17:32:56.016Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Scope note from the PR 1688 Codex review: removing userinfo must cover every spelling the URL parser normalizes, not only the literal '//user:secret@'. A backslash authority behind a wrapper, such as npm:https:\\user:secret@host, parses to the same credentials. pm-rrwh2o's carriesUrlCredentials, which parses each URL-scheme suffix with new URL, is the detection this item can reuse for redaction."}]}],"before_hash":"73bb8e8926183116cc9bd6e33405588f73b285a1d0fc41289cac9ec945a09c3d","after_hash":"4da670bf27b337a8e7e264eccf46e614f913bab2f706bc986511c4a542a9c49a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b898002aec49b56a8b80093eca9a444818e33ef50b67a3a8227a636b21c4aaec"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T18:35:02.049Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T18:35:02.048Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Correction to the earlier scope note: PR 1688 no longer ships carriesUrlCredentials. Four Codex rounds each found one more URL spelling the parser normalizes, so the retry guard became the conservative rule 'a token containing both @ and : may carry credentials'. For this item's redaction, which must rewrite tokens rather than withhold them, remove userinfo from a parse of a copy with tabs and newlines stripped, trying each scheme start. Where that cannot be proven, replace the whole token with a placeholder and drop the executable retry."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T18:35:02.049Z"}],"before_hash":"4da670bf27b337a8e7e264eccf46e614f913bab2f706bc986511c4a542a9c49a","after_hash":"df1f596d686177ac3cbc2a09b831ed3ccfae800123796a1baec13a94ffaa77f4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8675ff96a586e343c053e3c1e75ed879473874bb652f0e9b77a7797c6eae3fcd"}
