{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T12:59:49.442Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5htunt","claim:pm-gh1699","claim:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-5htunt","lineage:pm-5oj5","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-5htunt+pm-gh1699+pm-nhauur","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5htunt","claim:pm-gh1699","claim:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-5htunt","lineage:pm-5oj5","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T12:59:49.440Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation (branch fix/credential-shape-coverage): new src/core/shared/url-credentials.ts holds one conservative token rule: replace the span between a token's first ':' and its last '@' (after scheme slashes) with [redacted]. It is complete for every parser-normalized spelling for the same reason pm-rrwh2o's mayCarryUrlCredentials is. src/cli/runtime/refusal-credential-redaction.ts applies it once at emission, because many producers (unknown_option next_steps and examples, Commander retries recomputed at format time) echo the raw argv. It covers three paths: handleRunPmCliKnownError (context and message, before formatting, telemetry and Sentry), formatCommanderUsageJson (envelope, before lean projection and output-token accounting so the receipt measures the delivered bytes) and formatCommanderUsageMessage (text, before the help_format override). Each path replaces exact raw and both-shell-quoted spellings of every credential-bearing token and inline option value; this catches userinfo containing spaces. It applies the token rule to argv-token fields and the word rule to free text. When the retry text changes, suggested_retry and suggested_retry_args are withheld, and a next step tells the caller to restore the credentials. Verified with the built CLI: unknown_option (JSON and text), read_output_mutation_conflict (JSON and text), a space inside the password, a backslash authority and an inline --install= value all print zero secret bytes. Found while doing this: telemetry attempted_args leak userinfo whenever the host has no dot (filed pm-5htunt)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T12:59:49.442Z"}],"before_hash":"7392834c38ea7ba39ad19fade7f1ccfdb48c49de533646c584903cf02a32541f","after_hash":"8979fc5d6eba6c3d412db0f2b81117cc7b77aaccf1d1f7350272e6e5c9669eaf","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3e984d01c47518316d177f955ba561461efc3e8e5123d4d8e82f80713cf0c2f8"}
